  "published": "2026-10-18T19:13:19.183Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.0.2: Dependency refresh. Moves to CoreSystem.Resilience 2.0.3, which carries Polly 8.8.0, OpenTelemetry 1.20.0 and CoreSystem.Observability.Abstractions 1.0.2, and to CoreSystem.Serialization 1.2.4. No API changed, nothing is renamed, and no code changed: the entire difference is in the declared dependency versions. Projects on .NET 8 are unaffected by the refresh. Correction to the 3.0.1 notes, which stated that this package restores on .NET SDK 10 and later: that claim is false and was never verified. Tested against a real net10.0 consumer, Resilience 2.0.2 and 2.0.3 both fail restore with NU1605, because Resilience constrains Microsoft.Extensions.* to 8.0.x while OpenTelemetry asks for 10.0.0. Until CoreSystem.Resilience stops constraining them, a net10.0 consumer has to pin Microsoft.Extensions.* to 10.0.x directly. The two breaking changes introduced in 3.0.0 still apply, so migrating from 2.x means deleting any assignment to CacheOptions.MaxCacheableSize, referencing IExternalCacheStorage instead of ICacheTagIndex<T>, and removing any direct use of MemoryKeyTracker or DefaultRequestCachePolicy.",
